A blessed magic lamp is an 80% chance of a wish.  One that is
only uncursed only a 20% chance.  A blessed magic lamp only has
a 5% chance of generating a hostile genie; an uncursed one a 20%
chance.  If you're going to rub the lamp, you definitely should
bless it first.

> except that it provides an extra layer of protection against
> having them cursed by spellcasters. And it's just as easy to
> uncurse items as it is to bless them in advance.

Provided you have the holy water to do so at the time.  (But
this early in the game, I don't think cursing is a real risk,
and he'll have lots of holy water before it becomes a risk.  At
least, I always end up with a lot more than I need.)

